{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smart plug and newer Echo Dot feel like useful additions to my Fire TV setup because they add lamp control and hands-free Alexa access.",
    "The HDMI cable fits the TV equipment I use, although I would only buy it when I actually need another connection."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The recommended Fire TV sticks repeat a function my existing 4K stick already provides, so being closely related to my purchases does not make them useful next choices.",
    "The tablet, earbuds, and portable speaker do not address my current TV or home security needs, and I have no confirmed use for the memory card.",
    "The older Echo Dot is less appealing when the newer version on the same page serves my intended purpose."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire TV purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to recommend more streaming sticks, even though I already have that need covered.",
    "Interest in Alexa and electronics seems to have been stretched into interest in tablets and audio accessories without a clear connection to what I want to do next."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I care about whether a device adds a useful capability to what I already own, rather than duplicating it or offering less capability.",
    "My recent camera and TV purchases make practical additions to those setups more relevant than general electronics, but accessories still need a specific use or confirmed compatibility."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my Alexa and TV interests but missed the difference between extending my setup and repeating needs I have already covered."
}"}
